    "what_a_drifted_input_digest_means": "this block is NOT covered by design_sha256, so nothing here can change what was pre-registered.  A digest below that no longer matches the file on disk means the world moved since freezing, and for the runner's own digest it means the phases would execute something other than the code this design was frozen against -- so verify_manifest reports it, returns valid=False, and load_prereg refuses.  Re-freezing is the repair and is provably not a new pre-registration: it re-binds these inputs and leaves design_sha256 byte-identical, which is the property that distinguishes re-binding a design from changing one.  What is NOT repaired by re-freezing is a design_sha256 that no longer reproduces, because that means the design itself moved"
